# Sample configuration for the deacon-bot (TypeScript / NestJS) service.
#
#     cp env.example .env        dotenv reads `.env`, not this file
#     npx prisma generate        required unless `npm ci` already ran it
#
# WHY THIS FILE IS NOT NAMED `.env.example`
# The runtime snapshot did contain a `.env.example`, and it was reviewed. It
# carried the same placeholder token/chat values as below, but its DATABASE_URL
# named a private-range internal host address and a real database role name.
# This repository is public, so those two tokens were replaced with the local
# placeholders below; nothing else was changed. The harness also blocks writing
# any `.env*` path, which is why the conventional leading dot is absent here.
# See docs/RECONSTRUCTION.md section 6.
#
# Everything in this file is what the recovered code actually reads. No
# variable is listed here unless some src/*.ts file looks it up.

# --- Telegram ---------------------------------------------------------------
# BotFather token. Never commit a real one.
BOT_TOKEN='0000000000:REPLACE-ME-REPLACE-ME-REPLACE-ME'

# HelpUkraine supergroup id (negative, including the -100 prefix).
# Read by AnnouncementService for the scheduled closure message, with NO
# default: leave it unset and the job sends to `undefined`.
CHAT_ID='-1001234567890'

# MUST be 1.
#
# BotProvider does: new TelegramBot(token, { polling: Boolean(Number(x)) }).
# Nothing in the program opens a webhook or serves HTTP, so 0 (or unset) does
# NOT select another mode -- the process boots, schedules its cron job, logs
# "Bot started...", and then receives no updates at all, forever.
BOT_POLLING=1

# Has no effect as written.
# SilentTimeService computes: Boolean(Number(process.env.IS_BOT_SILENT)) || true
# which is `true` for every input, so this cannot be turned off, and the
# `!isSilent && console.log(...)` in that constructor is dead code. Kept
# because the recovered source reads it.
IS_BOT_SILENT=1

# --- Silent window ----------------------------------------------------------
# Compared against Date#getHours() of the message timestamp, i.e. the
# CONTAINER's local timezone -- not UTC, whatever the original sample implied.
# docker-compose.yaml sets no TZ, so the effective window depends on the host.
# Defaults if unset/0: too-early 6, too-late 23. Boundaries are inclusive:
# hours <= IS_TOO_EARLY and >= IS_TOO_LATE are silent.
IS_TOO_EARLY=5
IS_TOO_LATE=21

# --- Postgres ---------------------------------------------------------------
# DATABASE_URL must be set for the Prisma client to be generated and for the
# app to connect. SHADOW_DATABASE_URL is required by schema.prisma (a
# `shadowDatabaseUrl` datasource field) for `prisma migrate` to work.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://deacon:deacon@localhost:5432/deacon_bot?schema=public"
SHADOW_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://deacon:deacon@localhost:5432/deacon_bot_shadow?schema=public"

# --- Scheduled announcement -------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED, not optional. AnnouncementService reads it with
# `configService.get('GROUP_CLOSURE_ANNOUNCEMENT')` and passes the result
# straight to sendMessage with no default and no await, so an unset value
# means `undefined` is handed to the Telegram API on schedule.
#
# The value below is the exact string recovered from the runtime source,
# including the typo "прозклад" -- reproduce it verbatim if the point is to
# match what was running.
GROUP_CLOSURE_ANNOUNCEMENT="Шановні учасники! Група перемикається в режим читання на нічний час. Детальнішу інформацію про прозклад роботи нашої групи читайте у Правилах Групи (закріплені повідомлення)."

# There is deliberately no GROUP_OPENED_ANNOUNCEMENT / morning-unlock variable.
# The recovered program registers exactly one cron job,
# 'NightlyClosureAnnouncement'. No opening announcement exists in the code.
